WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.975
Start your bid review in Pipeline, under Needs
attention.

00:00:03.975 --> 00:00:05.989
This walkthrough uses training examples.

00:00:05.989 --> 00:00:10.017
Each row shows the responsible person, deadline, and
next action.

00:00:10.017 --> 00:00:14.044
Choose Due in seven days to focus on approaching
deadlines,

00:00:14.044 --> 00:00:17.669
then select a bid to see what needs doing.

00:00:18.769 --> 00:00:20.609
Read the source before acting.

00:00:20.609 --> 00:00:26.130
This bid has an assigned estimator and a recorded
proposal deadline, but pricing is incomplete.

00:00:26.130 --> 00:00:28.706
The next action opens the linked estimate.

00:00:28.706 --> 00:00:32.755
Make the change in the underlying workspace, then
return to Pipeline

00:00:32.755 --> 00:00:35.331
and refresh to load the latest information.

00:00:36.431 --> 00:00:39.011
Use No owner to find responsibility gaps.

00:00:39.011 --> 00:00:44.172
Select a bid to see why it needs attention and where
to assign someone.

00:00:44.172 --> 00:00:47.121
For work already assigned, return to Needs attention

00:00:47.121 --> 00:00:50.070
and choose a person in the Owner filter.

00:00:50.070 --> 00:00:53.019
Search also finds a bid, owner, or blocker.

00:00:54.119 --> 00:00:58.880
Review old dates keeps deadlines more than thirty
days past in a separate queue.

00:00:58.880 --> 00:01:01.601
Confirm the bid's status before changing a date.

00:01:01.601 --> 00:01:04.322
Incoming emails still need review in Bid Intake.

00:01:04.322 --> 00:01:06.703
Your Document board stays one click away.

00:01:06.703 --> 00:01:11.124
Use Pipeline to leave each bid with a clear owner
and next action.
